{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKh6Cu3TB8jBQme9RZLa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014X5NsWSXFfWNKCgEgSSLob","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/work/.ard/157/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nWhen a non-lead triage role claims a human-filed issue that was already admitted, the claim log reports the wrong reason. The fix is small and internal: add a reason value to the intake package, use it on the stored-admission path in the triage candidate builder, and add a test case. Admission behaviour and user-facing interfaces stay the same, so only the engineer needs to plan it.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: steps for the new reason constant, setting it on the stored-admission path in internal/triage/candidates.go, and the candidates test case.\n- worker engineer: small Go change with a unit test.\n\n## Open issues\n- The new reason string will appear in slog output. Check whether any docs or log-parsing tooling list the reason values.\n- A comment on the issue shows that an earlier lead attempt failed while pushing. That was a controller problem, not a problem with this routing.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1582,"cache_read_input_tokens":10668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1582},"output_tokens":39,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"388a2d75-c967-490a-946e-7425f577f8fd","uuid":"d2b72f2a-24df-4cf9-ba3d-1b7703952e88","timestamp":"2026-11-23T10:20:50.411Z","request_id":"req_011ChKh6CmrNn4vnCfvEjb2s"}
