{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKh6ZY2XvTFz3EJ7wnS5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #157 with status **done**: the engineer worker will make the change, and only the engineer triage role needs to plan it first. The routing is in `.ard/157/triage-lead.md`.\n\nThe issue is a wrong reason in a log line. When a role other than lead claims a human-filed issue that was already admitted, the claim is logged as `app-authored`. The cause is in `internal/triage/candidates.go:105`: every candidate starts with that reason, and the stored-admission path never changes it. The fix needs a new reason value in `internal/intake/intake.go`, that value set on the stored-admission path, and a new case in the candidates test.\n\nIt's internal logging only and doesn't change admission, a public interface or stored data, so it doesn't need architect, product-manager or documentation-planner. Those roles don't exist in this repo anyway. The only reviewer, eng-review, has no `when:` rule, so it will review the pull request without any extra routing.\n\nI noted two things for a maintainer in the file:\n- **Log output:** the new reason string will show up in the logs, so it's worth checking whether any docs or log-parsing tools list the reason values.\n- **Earlier failed run:** a comment on the issue shows the previous lead run failed while pushing. That was a controller problem and doesn't affect this routing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":12250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":579},"output_tokens":425,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"388a2d75-c967-490a-946e-7425f577f8fd","uui